a prison Warden who supposedly resigned  is still getting a paycheck the eight  news now investigators continue to  uncover problems inside Nevada prisons  Vanessa Murphy has this story you're  seeing here first  a spokesperson told us a prison Warden  resigned months ago then we obtained  timesheets and the department changed  its story and this guy gets to resign  and still collect a six-figure salary  William Hutchings was the warden at  Southern desert Correctional Center  while a riot took place there in  December the department tried to  downplay it in April the 8 news now  investigators uncovered how bad it was  two months later a Nevada prison  spokesperson said Hutchings resigned for  personal reasons his final date of  employment July 15th his salary  according to the department nearly 128  thousand dollars then recently these  timesheets were obtained by the  investigators showing 40-hour work weeks  for Hutchings from July to mid-september  approved by the now acting director the  department refused to confirm whether  Hutchins is still getting paid then on  Monday we received this reply Hutchings  will be employed until November 11th the  8 news now investigators also reached  out to the governor's office a  spokesperson responded the governor's  office cannot comment because  information regarding specific Personnel  issues are confidential the governor's  office is working close with the interim  director at endoc to address ongoing  issues for the benefit of staff and in  the interest of public safety director  Charles Daniels stepped down on Friday  at the request of the governor after The  Escape of a convicted murderer from the  same prison Southern desert Correctional  Center and after the 8 news now  investigators have exposed numerous  failures and concerns at the department  Paul lundquitz heads a union  representing correctional officers he  says he believes the Department's  actions surrounding the resignation of  Hutchings and these timesheets should be  investigated what was said behind closed  doors that that would allow something  like this to happen and what is the  department thinking and just  nonchalantly saying oh he's still  employed until this date you know how  how badly does that reflect on their the  leadership of our department and we  obtained an internal Memo from the  acting director of Nevada prisons he  acknowledged the uncertainty change in  senior leadership can cause and he said  staff will continue to focus on the  basics by exhibiting what right looks  like Vanessa Murphy 8 News Now  thank you Vanessa after the eight news  now investigators published this story  on 8newsnow.com a short while ago a  Nevada prison spokesperson sent an email  stating they have received clarification  and Hutchings is on paid administrative  leave
 

